tests:
pane.test.mjs (new), plus additions to runs.test.mjs and steps.test.mjs. Use the stub fetch, mock timers, and stubbed R.host from notes.test.mjs:649-659. Normalise \r\n in source scans.
- Two loops, two runs. The tab's watch('r2') plus a pane's follow('r1'): both runs are polled every 1 s while running, and neither stops the other. This test fails on today's single loop (runs.js:358-360).
- Reference count:
  - follow('r1') twice makes one detail request per pass;
  - one release keeps it polling, the second stops it;
  - a third release is a no-op.
- modelFor('r1') carries r1's v while the tab's `model` carries r2's.
- modelFor('r5') before any follow gives a signal holding null (the pane's first render), and modelFor('../x') gives null.
- poke('r1') makes one look at r1 only; poke() looks at the tab's run; answerRun('r1', '0') pokes r1's loop.
- The models cap: follow('r1'), then watch nine other rids in turn; modelFor('r1') still holds its reducer (lastId kept).
- Visibility:
  - the stub at runs.test.mjs:35 keeps ONE listener per event type and removes by type, so it cannot see a doubled or a leaked listener. It becomes a Set of functions per type, removed by function. Its two uses adapt: runs.test.mjs:136 fires every listener of the type, and :140 asserts that none is left;
  - hidden: no request from any loop;
  - openTab with the tab's watch('r2') and a pane's follow('r1'): one visibilitychange gives the tab's refresh once and exactly one detail and one log request per rid. It fails if openTab's `back` still pokes;
  - after the tab closes and every loop is released, no visibilitychange listener is left.
- toPane:
  - an open graph pane with the same key is focused, and openXPane is not called;
  - otherwise openXPane('graph', {chat:'c1', pick:'r4'}, {at: <inspected id>, dir: undefined});
  - 'new', '../x', 'turns' with chat null, and chat 'a/b' each return null with no host call;
  - (null, 'r4') and ('c1', 'r4') dedupe to one pane.
- The strip handlers:
  - auxclick button 1 calls onPane('r4');
  - auxclick button 2 does nothing;
  - mousedown button 1 is preventDefault'ed;
  - a ctrl click calls onPane, a plain click calls pick;
  - [ new run ] has no aux handler;
  - [ ⇱ pane ] is off with 'new' selected.
- Registration: paneKinds.get('graph') has Pane, title, status and cwd; rightTabs graph is still global.
- title and status: a chat titled with \u202e and '<script>' comes out cleaned and as text; a chat not in the list uses the id; no chat says 'no chat'.
- The body, by state, using GraphPane's pure chooser `paneBody({ p, chatPanes, list, trash, mode })`:
  - chat open: turns;
  - chat closed: 'not open here', where [ open it ] calls host.openCmd('open c1');
  - in trash: the trash sentence;
  - gone: 'this chat is gone';
  - a rid pane with the chat closed: run.
- cwd: a chat pane's hello.cwd, then the list row's cwd, then ''.
- graphItems:
  - for a chat pane c1: one 'graph' item whose sub is turns plus c1's runs, each calling toPane with at = p.id and the dir;
  - for a note pane: [];
  - under a door: turns only;
  - for a chat c9 with no cache entry: turns plus the greyed 'runs' line, and exactly one lane request runs?chat=c9 (a second call while it waits makes none); after the answer, the sub lists c9's runs.
- A refusal in the pane: answerRun('r1', '0') answered 503 {error:'the browser service is down'} puts that sentence in paneBody's RunView tree for r1, and noticeFor(notice, null), the tab's line, is null for it.
- steps.test.mjs: Steps for r1 with showAll toggled, then Steps for r2, draws r2 folded. It fails if showAll is global again.
- Source:
  - '../graph/pane.js' joins the rules list at runs.test.mjs:511;
  - pane.js has no `<button`, no innerHTML, no `fetch(`, no eval;
  - it has no `openTab(`, `R.picks`, `R.model` or `paneMenu`;
  - its hubPost calls go only to runs.
- Each new test must fail when its line of the change is reverted (check by hand once). The whole page suite passes once.
